  "term": "medial preoptic area",
  "definition": "The medial preoptic area (mPOA) is a brain region that influences how likely birds are to sing and how strongly they sing. In the source provided, it is linked to gregarious song in European starlings and shows molecular activity involving glutamate and dopamine pathways.",
